# Developer Guide

This guide is for people who work on {{ project_name }} itself.

## Setup

```bash
uv sync
make check        # ruff + pytest with bpy
make mkdocs       # serve these docs
```

`make help` lists every target. Ruff uses a line length of 89 and the `E`, `F` and `UP`
rules. Docstrings are Google style: the API reference is generated from them.

!!! important
    `import {{ package_slug }}` must work **outside Blender** (docs, tooling), so `bpy`
    is imported inside the functions that use it. Only the modules of `extension/` import
    `bpy` at the top, since Blender is the only one loading them.

